  --     divisible by p, and every x in X, s in S with x·s·m = 6·y for some 1 ≤ m ≤ 3, y < n, p ∤ y, gcd(m, y) = 1.
  --     Then |X| + |S| ≤ n − 1.  (Equality holds for X = {2, 3, 6}, S = {s < n : p ∤ s}: the hypotheses are satisfiable.)
